# NOTICE

## Hypodermic

This directory contains a vendored copy of **Hypodermic**, a header-only
Dependency Injection container for C++11.

- Upstream: https://github.com/TheranBryant/Hypodermic
- License: MIT (see `LICENSE` in this directory)
- Copyright (c) 2016 Theran Bryant
- Vendored state: last synced from upstream in 2017, unmaintained since

### Local modifications

Unlike upstream, this copy carries local changes that are **compile-time
optimizations only**. No public API, no behavior and no ABI-visible semantics
were changed; the modifications exist purely to reduce the preprocessed
header weight of the DI container, which is pulled into every translation unit
that implements or derives from `FeatureInterface`.

| File | Change | Rationale |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `include/Hypodermic/TypeInfo.h` | Dropped `#include <regex>`; replaced `boost::algorithm::replace_all_copy` with an inline loop | `<regex>` was only referenced from the non-GNUC branch, i.e. dead code on GCC/Clang/MSVC. `boost/algorithm/string.hpp` cost ~95 k preprocessed lines for a single 2-to-1 character replacement. |
| `include/Hypodermic/ComponentContext.h` | Replaced `boost::adaptors::reverse` with a `rbegin`/`rend` loop | `boost/range/adaptor/reversed.hpp` cost ~62 k preprocessed lines for one reverse iteration. |
| `include/Hypodermic/ResolutionContainer.h` | Replaced `boost::range::sub_range` with a standard-library range | `boost/range/sub_range.hpp` cost ~62 k preprocessed lines. |
| `include/Hypodermic/Signal.h` | Added a small `Hypodermic::Signal` replacement for `boost::signals2::signal` | `boost/signals2.hpp` was the single heaviest include at ~109 k preprocessed lines. |
| `include/Hypodermic/IRegistrationDescriptor.h`, `include/Hypodermic/RegistrationActivator.h` | Use `Hypodermic::Signal` instead of `boost::signals2::signal` | See `Signal.h`. Only the subset of the signals2 API that Hypodermic actually used is provided. |

Together these reduced the preprocessed weight of `Hypodermic/ContainerBuilder.h`
from ~151 k to ~75 k lines. See `../../ROADMAP.md` §4 for measurements.

If you re-sync this directory from upstream, re-apply the changes listed above.